doc.text:
The running IDE: created by the builder, extended by the installers
(editor, query, catalog, results and app parts) and then run. Field handle is an Opaque["harlequin.ide"] whose payload
is one dict[str, object] (the "shared state", S below) shared by every copy.
All reads and writes of S from worker threads happen while holding S["lock"];
after changing S a worker calls S["invalidate"](). Keys of S:
"app": the prompt_toolkit Application (full_screen=True, mouse_support=False);
"kb": the Application's prompt_toolkit KeyBindings;
"lock": a threading.RLock;
"settings": the HarlequinSettings; "context": the IdeContext;
"bound_handle": real.harlequin.keymap.BoundKeySet holding every active key;
"bound": the same tuple[real.harlequin.keymap.BoundKey, ...] unwrapped from
bound_handle.handle for local key dispatch; never pass this full tuple as a
List through another facade;
"connection": the open real.harlequin.adapters.Connection, or None;
"running": bool, a query batch is running;
"buffers": list of dicts {"title": str ("Tab N"), "buffer": a prompt_toolkit
Buffer (multiline, SQL)}; "active": int index of the shown buffer;
"tab_counter": int, last N used in a "Tab N" title;
"layout": real.harlequin.ide.LayoutState; "run_bar": real.harlequin.ide.RunBar;
"results": list of real.harlequin.results.ResultSet; "grids": list of
real.harlequin.results.ResultsGrid (one per result); "result_index": int;
"results_state": "empty" | "loading" | "ready";
"catalog": list of real.harlequin.catalog.CatalogEntry (the Databases tree);
"tree": real.harlequin.catalog.TreeState; "catalog_tab": "Databases" |
"Files" | "S3"; "files": list of CatalogEntry; "files_tree": TreeState;
"s3": list of CatalogEntry; "s3_tree": TreeState;
"completions": a real.harlequin.catalog.CompletionSet (build_ide starts it as
real.harlequin.catalog.completion_set(real.harlequin.catalog.builtin_completions()));
"notifications": list of real.harlequin.ide.Notification;
"dialog": None or a pair (kind: str, model: object) where kind is "text"
(TextModal), "input" (InputModal), "confirm" (ConfirmModal), "menu"
(ContextMenu), "export" (ExportDialog) or "history" (pair of HistoryScreen and
list of QueryRecord);
"handlers": dict[str, Callable[[], None]] mapping a full action name of
Harlequin's action catalog (for example
"code_editor.new_buffer") to the function that performs it; in the installer
docs a quoted handler name without a dot means the action with the pane
prefix of that installer ("code_editor." for the editor part,
"data_catalog." for the catalog part, "results_viewer." for the results
part, none for the query and app parts), and a pane-prefixed focus action
("code_editor.focus_results_viewer", ...) is registered by the app part like
its App-scope twin;
"dialog_keys": dict[str, Callable[[str, str], None]] mapping a dialog kind to
the function that receives (textual key name, typed text) while that dialog is
open;
"on_exit": list of Callable[[], None] run in order after a normal quit;
"on_crash": list of Callable[[], None] run after an unexpected exception;
services installed by the builder: "invalidate": Callable[[], None] (thread-safe
app.invalidate()); "notify": Callable[[str | None, str, str], None] taking
title, message and severity name "information" | "warning" | "error", which
appends a notification stamped with the monotonic time in ms;
"open_dialog": Callable[[str, object], None]; "close_dialog":
Callable[[], None]; "focus": Callable[[str], None] applying a layout action
name to "layout" and moving prompt_toolkit focus to the window of the
resulting pane; "size": Callable[[], tuple[int,
int]] giving the terminal (columns, rows);
services installed by the editor part: "new_buffer":
Callable[[str], None] (open a new "Tab N" buffer with the text and focus it);
"insert_text": Callable[[str], None] (insert at the active buffer's cursor and
focus the editor); "selection": Callable[[], tuple[str, int, int]] (active
buffer text, selection anchor and cursor as character offsets);
services installed by the query part: "run_statements":
Callable[[list[str]], None] (run statements as a query batch, the way
run_query does); "refresh_catalog": Callable[[], None].
A handler or service that is not installed is simply absent from S.
